// REJECTS: Unsupported Milestoning type 'temporal'
//
// The milestoning entry rule is deliberately shapeless: `milestoningType PAREN_OPEN
// milestoningSpecification PAREN_CLOSE`, where the type is any identifier and the body is
// `(relationalIdentifier | COMMA | BOOLEAN | DATE | EQUAL)*` -- a token soup that matches
// nearly anything balanced. `business` and `processing` are not in the grammar at all.
//
// They are supplied by registered extensions, and the source text is RE-PARSED by whichever
// one claims the type name. So the whole of milestoning is invisible to the .g4: a rewrite
// that implements the rule as written accepts `temporal(...)`, `foo(BAR = BAZ)` and the
// snapshot/range mixture pinned in exclusive-snapshot-and-range.pure.
//
// Pinning the message matters more here than anywhere else in this corpus. This is exactly
// the shape of the packaging gap described in the README -- a missing extension makes every
// milestoning type report "Unsupported Milestoning type", so a fixture asserting only "was
// rejected" would keep passing while `business` quietly stopped working.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::UnknownMilestoningType
(
   Table T
   (
      milestoning
      (
         temporal(SOME_DATE = SNAP)
      )
      ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY,
      SNAP DATE
   )
)
